---
import ConverterPage from '../components/ConverterPage.astro';
---

<ConverterPage
  path="/devlys-to-unicode"
  lede="Paste DevLys 010 text on the left and get Unicode Hindi on the right, once the DevLys layout has been verified."
>
  <h2>Close to Kruti Dev, and that is the problem</h2>
  <p>
    DevLys 010 shares almost all of its keyboard layout with Kruti Dev 010. The
    engine already has a DevLys map seeded from the Kruti Dev one, and it would
    convert the great majority of text correctly: matras, reph, the common
    conjuncts, all of it.
  </p>
  <p>
    The trouble is the minority. Where the two layouts diverge, the output is
    not obviously broken: it is fluent-looking Hindi with a few letters quietly
    replaced. That is worse than a visible failure, because there is nothing to
    alert you. So the page stays off until the two layouts have been diffed
    against real DevLys documents and the differences are covered by tests.
  </p>
  <p>
    If your document is actually Kruti Dev, <a href="/">Kruti Dev to Unicode</a>
    is finished and tested.
  </p>
</ConverterPage>
